4. Results
Fig. 8 depicts the proportions of glances to each AoI, over time, across all driving conditions. Distinctions can be observed between different driving conditions. Generally, the gaze distribution during the manual drive was relatively stable, except for the period around the Cutoff Point, which indicated that the road event (the off-ramp and cones) altered drives’ gaze patterns. While for L2 and L3 drives, the gaze dis­ tribution evolved diversly with time (after TORs), which was also affected by the length of time budget. More specific presentations are shown in three sections: (1) Before TORs, (2) After TORs, and (3) Gaze polling behaviours.
4.1. Before TORs
