5. Discussion
5.1. An integrated gaze control model during take-over driving
The current study investigated drivers’ gaze behaviours across manual driving, L2, and L3 automated driving conditions, as well as the subsequent gaze patterns during the transition of control, under different time budgets. To have a better understanding of the observa­ tions, the conceptual gaze control model, as highlighted in Section 1.1, given by Shiferaw et al. (2019), was extended in this study by incor­ porating some components reflecting the circumstance of take-over driving (see Fig. 16 for schematic depiction, new components incorpo­ rated in this study were highlighted in yellow blocks). In this framework, gaze control is a prediction process, based on the interaction of bottom-

